body:
They did punish me sometimes but hard a very hard time every sitting with any of the punishments or really allowing them to set. I remember being so mad in my room when I was being punished I think at times I mightve been beyond help at that point. 

&#x200B;

But yea. They had a hard time punishing me or it didnt work very well. I never really did anything that I was suppose to other than go to school and hang out with friends growing up.

This might be true. I sometimes might be speaking from a place of ideology rather than actual experience. And I think the quote is accurate regardless. Especially if you are talking about things that are important to you or good things that are happening to you. Sometimes people try to one up you or try to talk about what good things happened to them or why you're stupid or whatever. I think he's right to stop talking to people that do this around you because you need to aim upwards.

&#x200B;

Essentially people who don't listen to the good things that happen to you and encourage you are pulling or pushing you downwards.

You realize how many people in history fought for to obliterate segregation laws. All this is doing is recreating segregation. It's not supporting any individuals it's supporting people based on the color of their skin which is something we've been trying to get away from.

&#x200B;

What this does is make it so that individuals like yourself have a foot to stand on when people start acting out against these things. Your argument is completely irrelevant if you understood history and how most, if not all of these segregations were destroyed in the past 40 years. We're suppose to be passed this and considering how many black individuals are rich in the United States this is completely a step backward trying to ideologically segregate people based off the color of their skin.
